## Examples (Ví dụ)

### Ví dụ 1: API Endpoint Review

**Code under review:**

```typescript
// POST /api/users
async function createUser(req, res) {
  const { email, name, password } = req.body;
  
  const user = await db.query(
    `INSERT INTO users (email, name, password) 
     VALUES ('${email}', '${name}', '${password}')`
  );
  
  res.json({ user });
}
```

**Review comments:**

```typescript
// MUST-FIX #1: SQL Injection Vulnerability
// Attacker can inject malicious SQL through email or name fields
// Example attack: email = "' OR '1'='1"
// FIX: Use parameterized queries

async function createUser(req, res) {
  const { email, name, password } = req.body;
  
  // Input validation
  if (!isValidEmail(email)) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid email' });
  }
  
  // Hash password
  const hashedPassword = await bcrypt.hash(password, 12);
  
  // Parameterized query
  const user = await db.query(
    `INSERT INTO users (email, name, password_hash) 
     VALUES ($1, $2, $3) 
     RETURNING *`,
    [email, name, hashedPassword]
  );
  
  res.status(201).json({ data: user });
}
```

### Ví dụ 2: React Component Review

**Code under review:**

```typescript
function UserList({ users }) {
  const [selectedId, setSelectedId] = useState(null);
  
  return (
    <div>
      {users.map(user => (
        <UserCard 
          key={user.id}
          user={user}
          onClick={() => setSelectedId(user.id)}
        />
      ))}
      {selectedId && <UserDetail id={selectedId} />}
    </div>
  );
}
```

**Review comments:**

```
SHOULD-FIX #1: Performance - Missing memoization
- UserList re-renders on any parent re-render
- UserCards re-render unnecessarily

SUGGESTION #1: Use React.memo for UserCard
const UserCard = React.memo(function UserCard({ user, onClick }) {
  // ...
});

SHOULD-FIX #2: State management
- selectedId should be lifted if needed by parent
- Consider if this is local UI state or app state

NIT #1: Consider extracting key extraction
- Use key={user.id} is correct, but could be explicit
```

## Anti Pattern

- [ ] **Rubber Stamping**: Approving without actual review
- [ ] **Personal Attacks**: Making it about the person, not code
- [ ] **Nitpicking Everything**: Focusing on style over substance
- [ ] **Missing Context**: Reviewing code in isolation
- [ ] **No Action**: Reviewing but not leaving feedback
- [ ] **Late Reviews**: Reviewing after too many changes
- [ ] **Blocking Trivialities**: Rejecting for minor issues
- [ ] **Inconsistent Standards**: Different standards for different people

## Best Practice

- [ ] **Timely Reviews**: Review within 24-48 hours
- [ ] **Be Constructive**: Focus on improvement, not criticism
- [ ] **Explain Why**: Don't just say "wrong", explain why
- [ ] **Suggest Solutions**: Don't just point out problems
- [ ] **Use Severity Labels**: Help author prioritize
- [ ] **Praise Good Code**: Acknowledge well-written sections
- [ ] **Consider Author Perspective**: Understand their intent
- [ ] **Be Consistent**: Apply same standards to all PRs

